From: David Aerne <meodai@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell: avoid the grouped Binding form in the config window

Opening a containment's configuration page segfaults plasmashell.

AppletConfiguration.qml sets the config window's flags and visibility with a
grouped-target Binding:

    Binding {
        root.Window.window.flags: Qt.FramelessWindowHint
        root.Window.window.visibility: Window.Maximized
    }

Evaluating that form crashes inside QQmlBind on our Qt 6.11.2 build:

    #1 QV4::ExecutionEngine::toVariant                     <- SEGV_MAPERR
    #3 QQmlBind::eval
    #4 QQmlBind::componentComplete
    #5 QQmlObjectCreator::finalize
    #9 PlasmaQuick::ConfigView::setSource
    #13 Plasma::Containment::configureRequested

The exact cause is unknown. A null Window.window was ruled out: that path logs
`Unknown name "root.Window.window.flags"` and drops the binding rather than
crashing, and no such line appears in the journal. A `when:` guard does not
help either - componentComplete evaluates the grouped form regardless of the
condition (verified on the device, with the patched file confirmed loaded).
A libplasma/Qt ABI mismatch is the current suspicion.

Assigning the properties directly avoids QQmlBind altogether. Flags are set
before visibility so the window is frameless before it maps. Component.onCompleted
covers the case where libplasma has already parented the item into its window, in
which case onWindowChanged fired before we could connect to it.

Reproduced on a Retroid Pocket 6 (aarch64, sm8550) running the folio
homescreen: long-press the homescreen, tap Settings. Five identical
backtraces before the change; none after, and the config page still opens
frameless and maximized.
---
--- a/shell/contents/configuration/AppletConfiguration.qml
+++ b/shell/contents/configuration/AppletConfiguration.qml
@@ -59,12 +59,22 @@
         }
     }
 
-    Binding {
-        // Window bindings
-        root.Window.window.flags: Qt.FramelessWindowHint
-        root.Window.window.visibility: Window.Maximized
+    // The grouped Binding form crashes QQmlBind::eval on our Qt build; the exact cause is
+    // unknown. Assigning directly skips QQmlBind, and sets flags before visibility so the
+    // window is frameless before it maps. onWindowChanged alone will not do: libplasma may
+    // parent this into the window before completion, so the signal has already fired.
+    function applyWindowState() {
+        const win = root.Window.window;
+        if (!win) {
+            return;
+        }
+        win.flags = Qt.FramelessWindowHint;
+        win.visibility = Window.Maximized;
     }
 
+    Component.onCompleted: root.applyWindowState()
+    Window.onWindowChanged: root.applyWindowState()
+
     Component {
         id: configurationKcmPageComponent
         ConfigurationKcmPage {}
